      "content": "I'm currently reviewing our Q3 expense reports for the manufacturing branch in Stuttgart. I've noticed some recurring, small-scale discrepancies in the 'miscellaneous office supplies' ledger. They aren't large enough to trigger a full forensic audit flag, but they are irregular and don't match our standard procurement cycles. Can you suggest a systematic method for investigating these types of minor, persistent anomalies without escalating the situation unnecessarily?",
